  {"type": "split", "h2": "Why we price a heat pump next to every big AC repair in Ottawa", "photo": "sys",
   "html": "<p>When an AC repair in Ottawa involves a compressor or a coil on a unit older than twelve years, we price a cold-climate heat pump beside it. Not as an upsell. In a city with -25°C winters and sticky summers, it's the one piece of equipment that earns its keep twelve months a year.</p><p>Here's the logic. A heat pump cools exactly like a central air conditioner: same outdoor unit, same indoor coil, same ducts. The difference is a reversing valve that lets it pull heat from outside air in winter. A Midea EVOX G3 or Kepler unit is rated to -30°C, so it carries most of the heating season on Hydro Ottawa rates and hands off to your Enbridge gas furnace below the balance point we set. Your furnace drops to a supporting role for the deep freeze.</p><p>The money works too. The install starts at $5,500, and qualifying units can bring back up to $7,500 through the Home Renovation Savings Program, commonly up to $2,000 for a gas-heated home. A plain AC replacement gets no rebate. If you'd rather repair, or replace like for like, we do that without a sales pitch. Either way the numbers sit on one sheet, and our <a href='/ottawa/'>Ottawa heating and cooling page</a> covers the full picture.</p>"},
